From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Meridian <meridian@localhost>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 15:09:02 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: a page that saves on the way out isn't put to sleep
 (Discord stays signed in)

Discord takes its sign-in out of localStorage while it is open and writes it
back in beforeunload. Auto-sleep (and Put to Sleep) is Chromium's discard,
which runs no beforeunload: after a tab fell asleep, Discord opened signed
out.

A tab whose page has a beforeunload handler (WebContents::
NeedToFireBeforeUnload) now stays awake, for auto-sleep and for Put to
Sleep, which says why ("the site saves when it is closed"). Not
NeedToFireBeforeUnloadOrUnloadEvents(): it counts visibilitychange too,
which nearly every site has and which already ran when the tab went to the
background; running the handlers before the discard isn't possible either
(pagehide and unload only run with ClosePage, which closes the tab).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 chrome/browser/meridian/sidebar_handler.cc               | 9 +++++++++
 .../browser/resources/webui_browser/meridian/sidebar.ts  | 1 +
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/meridian/sidebar_handler.cc b/chrome/browser/meridian/sidebar_handler.cc
index acfff79abb..5c117077e2 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/meridian/sidebar_handler.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/meridian/sidebar_handler.cc
@@ -555,6 +555,15 @@ std::string SidebarHandler::WhyAwake(tabs::TabInterface* tab) {
   if (page && (page->HadFormInteraction() || page->HadUserEdits())) {
     return "form";
   }
+  // A page that saves on the way out (Discord takes its sign-in out of
+  // localStorage while open and writes it back in beforeunload): sleep is a
+  // discard, which runs no such handler, so it would lose that. (Not
+  // NeedToFireBeforeUnloadOrUnloadEvents(): it counts visibilitychange too,
+  // which nearly every site has, and which already ran when the tab went to
+  // the background.)
+  if (contents->NeedToFireBeforeUnload()) {
+    return "unload";
+  }
   return std::string();
 }
 
diff --git a/chrome/browser/resources/webui_browser/meridian/sidebar.ts b/chrome/browser/resources/webui_browser/meridian/sidebar.ts
index 07c319f196..9dbabd163a 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/resources/webui_browser/meridian/sidebar.ts
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/webui_browser/meridian/sidebar.ts
@@ -2448,6 +2448,7 @@ export class MeridianSidebarElement extends CrLitElement implements
     const why: Record<string, string> = {
       'active': 'Not put to sleep: it is the open tab',
       'form': 'Not put to sleep: something typed on the page would be lost',
+      'unload': 'Not put to sleep: the site saves when it is closed (asleep, it could sign you out)',
       'media': 'Not put to sleep: it is playing sound or video',
       'capture': 'Not put to sleep: it uses the camera, microphone or a screen share',
       'workbench': 'Not put to sleep: the Workbench runs agent sessions',
